"240":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","270":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","30":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","300":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","330":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","60":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","90":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--1","properties":[["name","Log into Citrix server with compromised credentials"],["description","In this case, the threat actors used compromised credentials to log into an Internet-facing Citrix server to gain access to the network."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0001","technique":"T1078"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Use endpoint management platform for lateral movement"],["description","CTU researchers discovered evidence that the threat actors were not only leveraging the company\u2019s remote access infrastructure, but were also using the company\u2019s endpoint management platform, , to move laterally through the network (see Figure 1)."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0008","technique":"T1219"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","Run commands from recycler"],["description","CTU researchers immediately recognized suspicious commands, such as changing the working directory to recycler and executing commands from that location, that were unlikely to have been connected to legitimate system administrator operations."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0002","technique":"T1059.003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","Use PsExec to spawn remote shells"],["description","The results also revealed indications that PsExec, a popular system administration tool for executing commands on remote systems, was run against several target hosts to spawn shells on them."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0008","technique":"T1569.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a469636c-0cb2-50b9-92f9-644c8aa98197","120":"instance--d57b3a21-e910-5879-8148-40165cea451a","150":"instance--58250ef4-5bb4-5bf3-b33e-89493bbb395d","180":"instance--3e769cf2-c1e5-5d2e-81d4-892f48ce4d86","210":"instance--f6499e41-749c-5d7f-9346-96c08d0d5dfd","240":"instance--d9dcdfc8-5f42-546a-803a-0efcd5d4cf91","270":"instance--c9afd0f6-97ce-57b2-9d60-3557b6214809","30":"instance--75f82155-f5ff-5619-8bf8-aae22937cab0","300":"instance--25e2d26e-1b35-56bd-b9aa-096c2d3b0e3c","330":"instance--e0483688-da10-5376-8cf2-050bcc3b70f0","60":"instance--1293d9cc-16b2-5c67-a453-bd144aab133a","90":"instance--2b43cd52-10db-5b15-8ad5-c4b59496528b"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--5","properties":[["name","Map network drives with compromised Altiris account"],["description","The relevant strings inside the VAD sections were UTF-16 encoded and revealed additional insights once extracted. TG-1314 was mapping network drives using a compromised Altiris account to connect to additional systems (see Figure 5)."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0008","technique":"T1021.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--54fc1f38-f4e3-523e-b07c-73889b0d8df7","120":"instance--9cf45948-7040-5d7a-a1d5-3cb4db0c1af6","150":"instance--13bb13cc-e02b-51d2-8d7d-40e5613b6e5a","180":"instance--e33bc6ee-771e-54fe-a772-74dfdaad420d","210":"instance--286f51a3-8fc6-55ec-978e-8b05ebda3655","240":"instance--14659696-be77-5460-beb1-4b5eac126e43","270":"instance--f48ed1a6-2895-5cd2-9b1c-e30ac2bc8921","30":"instance--7b803e61-16ac-5720-92cd-8f2a456a52b7","300":"instance--76c24361-5143-5c43-8e4d-707c619e6038","330":"instance--f395cfc7-395a-5001-9552-a4fec6dbc53a","60":"instance--760885bb-9294-5a5b-93a2-a410e1ea4112","90":"instance--8e0d1a12-8611-598d-9a7d-40f2525e4781"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--6","properties":[["name","Leverage Altiris platform with compromised domain credentials"],["description","These results indicated that the threat actors leveraged the Altiris management platform installed at the client site, along with compromised domain credentials associated with the Altiris system, to move laterally within the compromised environment."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0008","technique":"T1219"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ac41cfc8-b0c0-554d-95b2-720150a5bf36","120":"instance--81db50a9-8784-5222-b3b9-11e79866e762","150":"instance--f6f023e9-8c93-517f-957f-31dca0d2a15b","180":"instance--894f0340-3886-5127-8a8f-0f6209d68771","210":"instance--610142b3-ced1-5867-9756-3a589320c39b","240":"instance--d3be45dc-b7ec-5e5f-8f62-7d3cd44224a0","270":"instance--a24bec77-859d-5e6b-bd5a-4086e7a7a234","30":"instance--dd7163a0-026e-5399-8486-9bbd3675d11f","300":"instance--acdfb49e-9f09-528d-82a1-1ce1a8054bc0","330":"instance--2f3b58b4-659c-535a-a85b-902cddeeab1a","60":"instance--de18780a-e8d0-5816-872b-99c26513088f","90":"instance--dfa61bc9-7a98-5381-8adf-c5170b709da3"},"id":"software","instance":"software--citrix-server","properties":[["vendor","Citrix"],["evidence",[["item-1",{"excerpt":"In this case, the threat actors used compromised credentials to log into an Internet-facing Citrix server to gain access to the network.","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20150626073312/http:/www.secureworks.com/resources/blog/living-off-the-land/"}]]],["display_name","Citrix server"],["name","Citrix server"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4613da28-bc93-582d-96e9-176cd23741c5","120":"instance--83b89aec-9b51-5c0c-8eb9-e4633bd85f3a","150":"instance--2b584ded-323d-53bf-a540-ab3f327ecebb","180":"instance--b16e7dcc-a411-579d-841d-bc81bc1f2f48","210":"instance--7762d27d-e89b-5ee4-9201-aa27f50008d0","240":"instance--1f0733e3-6582-5834-ae81-27a24d737870","270":"instance--817525a9-b4ce-5f5a-a37d-e56f09329bba","30":"instance--4033e97f-6145-5489-924d-7dc73ffc8c25","300":"instance--da1b46bc-df83-52c8-9a65-40137174210e","330":"instance--97177eb0-959b-58aa-a5c8-690be7b1da71","60":"instance--db48265c-680b-5425-954a-47bf87092043","90":"instan